# Copy to scripts/private-patterns.local (gitignored) and add one literal
# substring per line. The private-data check fails if any line appears in the
# scanned tree. Use this for machine-specific names that must never ship —
# e.g. MCP server names from your personal opencode/codex config, or a client
# project codename. Do not commit the real values; that re-ships the disclosure.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Caution: ordinary English words false-positive. Prefer scoped patterns
# (JSON keys like `"my-server":`) over bare words that also appear in UI copy.
#
# Example (placeholders only — replace with your own):
# my-client-mcp
# "server-from-my-config":
